head: 80 cases, 25 distinct templates
   12 x What was revenue in <year> <quarter>?
   12 x How many orders were there in <year> <quarter>?
   12 x What was gross margin in <year> <quarter>?

tail: 40 cases, 40 distinct templates
    1 x What is the racked storage capacity at the Dallas depot?
    1 x What is the total capacity of the Columbus depot?
    1 x What was utilisation at the Columbus depot at year end?

The largest template alone is 12 of 80 head cases. Cases that share
a phrasing tend to pass or fail together — one prompt, one tool, one kind of number —
so they carry less independent evidence than their count suggests, and an interval
computed as if every case were independent, like the one in 02, is too narrow.
